From 47dea790886052f15be2c2b6e409393840308d53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ross Lagerwall <ross.lagerwall@citrix.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Jul 2025 15:21:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Add xen_boot module for x86_64_efi

Add new loader for booting Xen on EFI platforms (currently only x86_64).
The loader presents the same command interface as the xen_boot loader
for ARM64.

The loader works by booting Xen as an EFI binary (similar to Linux)
while exposing an EFI Simple Filesystem Protocol for Xen to retrieve its
modules and associated information. Xen on EFI already has support for
retrieving the modules and information in this way so no changes are
needed to Xen.

This loader is needed to be allow booting Xen with Secure Boot enabled
since Multiboot does not support PE binaries.

Signed-off-by: Ross Lagerwall <ross.lagerwall@citrix.com>
diff --git a/grub-core/Makefile.core.def b/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
index b3f71196aaf0..e67864e04010 100644
--- a/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
+++ b/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
@@ -1848,7 +1848,9 @@ module = {
 module = {
   name = xen_boot;
   arm64 = loader/arm64/xen_boot.c;
+  x86_64_efi = loader/efi/xen_boot.c;
   enable = arm64;
+  enable = x86_64_efi;
 };
 
 module = {
diff --git a/grub-core/loader/efi/xen_boot.c b/grub-core/loader/efi/xen_boot.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..776240fbd03f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/grub-core/loader/efi/xen_boot.c
@@ -0,0 +1,765 @@
